# Publishable ViraUI skills authoring

Consumer skills live in sibling repo **`../viraui-skills`** ([vira-soft/viraui-skills](https://github.com/vira-soft/viraui-skills)), not under `packages/skills`.

Editing skills? **Read owning spec first**, then follow the Agent Skills checklist.

## Required flow

1. Read [skills-package.md](docs/specs/skills-package.md) §4 registry row and §7 (Agent Skills format + checklist).
2. Follow [agentskills.io](https://agentskills.io/skill-creation/quickstart) guidance: thin hub, trigger-only description, progressive disclosure into sibling refs.
3. **RED before GREEN:** write or refresh `../viraui-skills/evals/<skill>/trigger_queries.json` and `evals.json` **before** editing `SKILL.md`.
4. Hub `description`: starts `Use when…`, ≤ 1024 chars, **triggers/symptoms only** — no workflow summary (see [optimizing-descriptions](https://agentskills.io/skill-creation/optimizing-descriptions)).
5. Hub frontmatter: `name`, `description`, then `license: MIT` and `metadata` (`author: Vira Software`, `version` semver string).
6. Hub body ~80–120 lines: router + hard contract + out of scope; refs are load-on-demand (“Read `foo.md` when …”).
7. Same change: update spec §4 registry when action/trigger changes; discipline skills need red-flag + rationalization tables.
8. Evals stay under `../viraui-skills/evals/<skill>/` — **never** under `skills/`.

Contract: [skills-package §7](docs/specs/skills-package.md#7-authoring-rules).

## Before done

- Diff description against `trigger_queries.json` (true triggers vs near-miss false).
- Confirm hub frontmatter has `license: MIT` and `metadata.author` / `metadata.version`.
- Confirm consumer install docs still cite `npx skills add vira-soft/viraui-skills`.
- Run format check in `viraui-skills` for markdown edits.

## Red flags — STOP

- “Skip evals — small hub tweak”
- “Put evals next to SKILL.md under `skills/`”
- “Description can summarize the workflow — agents read the body anyway”
- “Registry update later”
- “Document npm `@viraui/skills` / tarball install”

**All of these mean: complete §7 checklist in this change.**
